Write ROLLOVER-LAUNCHED BEFORE calling the launcher; keep the nohup/& form. context-watch.py fires the same command only as a BACKUP. Never hand Jordan a prompt to paste; never wait for him. If auth is not True: `say -r 190 "Claude CLI is logged out, run claude login"`, record it as a HUMAN GATE in HANDOFF/STATUS, and run only the next atomic step as a fresh-context fable-high background subagent, re-probing auth every turn.

## Step 3 — The work, in strict order

**B1. EIN — TODAY. This is the pin holding the whole lane shut.** Free, ~10 min, IRS online, issued immediately. Prepare everything Jordan needs (entity name, entity number 5671365, responsible party, address, NAICS) so his part is typing. **HUMAN GATE: Jordan on the IRS site.** Evidence: EIN letter PDF on disk → `FACTS.md ein: VERIFIED`.

**B2. Business bank account.** Needs the EIN letter + the Ohio filing. Assemble the document packet; Jordan opens it. **Why it matters:** commingling — customer deposits into a personal account — is the most reliable way an Ohio LLC's liability shield gets pierced, and a 50% roof deposit is exactly that fact pattern. It also makes bookkeeping reconstructable and stops a five-figure deposit check being written to a personal name. **HUMAN GATE.** → `FACTS.md`.

**B3. Columbus BZS Home Improvement Contractor registration + $25k surety bond.** Assemble the checklist: notarized application, 767 exam (70%+), $185 fee, bond quote. Bond and insurance both want the FEIN. **HUMAN GATES: notarization, exam, spend.** → `FACTS.md bond`, `columbus_bzs_reg`.

**B4. Dublin registration — resolve UNKNOWN.** One call to Dublin's building department. Delegate the research to sonnet-medium; Jordan makes the call. Record the answer verbatim with the date and who said it. → `FACTS.md dublin_reg: VERIFIED or N/A`.

**B5. GL insurance signature.** Atlantic Casualty via Amy Blackstone; needs the FEIN. **HUMAN GATE: Jordan signs.** → `FACTS.md gl_policy`. Also open BWC if there will be employees.

**B6. SPF / DKIM / DMARC, then `info@` + `claims@`.** Draft the exact records; Jordan applies them at Cloudflare and in the Workspace admin console.
- SPF (TXT, apex): `v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all`
- DKIM: generate the key in Workspace Admin → Apps → Google Workspace → Gmail → Authenticate email, publish the `google._domainkey` TXT, then **turn authentication on**.
- DMARC (TXT, `_dmarc`): `v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:jordan@matchworkroofing.com`
**Then send a real test to `jordan@` and confirm receipt** — receipt is currently UNKNOWN and MX existing does not prove delivery. **This blocks Lane A's contact form**: a form emailing from an unauthenticated domain lands in spam and permanently trains Google to distrust the domain. **HUMAN GATES: every DNS record, every Workspace change.** Evidence: `dig TXT` from 1.1.1.1 **and** 8.8.8.8 before and after; a test send from each mailbox passing DMARC.

**B7. Realtor desk number.** A dedicated OpenPhone number auto-forwarding to Jordan with its own greeting, for the Close-Ready realtor program. Costs nothing, makes the "desk" real, and gives clean attribution. → `FACTS.md` **before** Lane A publishes it.

**B8. GBP — create as a Service-Area Business.** **Blocked on the interim logo** (see B9).
- Legal name **exactly** "Matchwork Roofing LLC". **No keyword stuffing.**
- **Address hidden from day one** — required for a home-based business with no walk-in customers; showing it is a suspension trigger. Never toggle it visible "to see how it looks". Real home address for backend verification only; **never a UPS/mailbox address**.
- Service area = **real drive-time coverage, Dublin core + greater Columbus**. Not statewide — overreach reads as spam and suppresses ranking. Expect distant ZIPs to rank weaker. Re-tune once the first jobs show the real radius.
- Primary category **Roofing contractor**; secondaries **Siding contractor**, **Gutter service**, **Masonry contractor**. No more.
- **Build the entire profile in one sitting** — piecemeal name/category/address edits in the first days are a review trigger.
- **Video verification:** one continuous take, 60–120 s — house exterior → the branded vehicle open with tools and ladder visible → signage or paperwork. **No faces, no voices.** Budget 1–2 weeks after submission; do not panic-edit while pending.
- Expect **Local Pack and Maps eligibility, but no public map pin and no directions button** — that is correct and expected for a hidden-address SAB.
**HUMAN GATE: Jordan submits.** → `FACTS.md`.

**B9. Interim logo on a vehicle magnet or yard sign.** Lane A produces the wordmark; Jordan picks and buys. **This is the GBP blocker** — there is nothing "branded" to film without it. **HUMAN GATE: print spend.**

**B10. Reviews.** Only actual paying **Matchwork Roofing LLC** customers. **Friends and former-employer (RSO/Feazel) clients: NO** — policy violation and a filter risk on a young profile. **No incentives of any kind** — no discount, gift, gift card or perk tied to leaving or editing a review, ever. Cap at **2–4 per week**, staggered. Direct Google review link, sent **2–5 days after completion**, open-ended ask, no suggested wording. If Google posts a warning banner or pauses reviews, **stop soliciting immediately** and let it cool. **HUMAN GATE: every request to a real person.**

**B11. Weekly GBP cadence.** 2–3 real job photos/week + ~1 Google Post/week (completed job, seasonal tip, service highlight), from Jordan's own Matchwork jobs, labeled via the `roofing-photo-id` + gallery-vocab stack (~$0.51/1k photos; **not yet wired to posting** — captions by hand until it is). **Do not hand-craft EXIF geotags — Google strips them.** The signal is steady real activity.

**B12. CertainTeed rep call.** Zero documentation exists on tier or SureStart PLUS — this is a phone call, not research. File whatever the rep provides. **The site may not name a tier until the document is on disk.** → `FACTS.md certainteed_tier`, `surestart_plus`.

**B13. Define the workmanship warranty for real, then have it reviewed.** Today it is a marketing phrase. Decide the actual term and what it covers (repair-only until the business lane secures more), get **ATTORNEY** review of the wording, then replace the placeholder. → `FACTS.md workmanship_warranty`.

**B14. Contract to the attorney.** Send `deliverables/MATCHWORK-CONTRACT-v1.pdf` together with the storm inspection letter and the warranty wording as one packet. **ATTORNEY GATE.** Ohio HSSA note: **mishandling the 3-day notice is the most common consumer-law exposure for home-improvement sellers** — two copies of the detachable Notice of Cancellation, dates filled in, handed to the buyer before leaving the home.

**B15. Financing.** No lender signed → **no financing copy anywhere on the site** (§0 ban). If Jordan signs one, it goes into `FACTS.md` first.

